# Netlify response headers.
#
# Defence in depth for the internal paths blocked in _redirects. Those rules
# return a forced 404, so in normal operation nothing here is ever reached —
# these headers exist so that if a force flag is dropped, a new internal
# directory is added without a matching rule, or a path is otherwise missed,
# the material still does not enter a search index.
#
# Keep this list in step with the "Internal paths: not published" block in
# _redirects.
#
# Nothing here applies to /LICENSE.md, /README.md, /DATA-RIGHTS.md or
# /THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, which are published deliberately, nor to any page
# route or to the /css/, /js/ and /images/ assets.

/site-strategy.md
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/seo-content-plan.md
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/seo-implementation.md
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/link-preservation-audit.md
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/docs/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/scripts/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/content/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/startups-app/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/data/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
